What this covers:

  data/regions/__generated__/   the derived seasons each poster is drawn from
  data/regions/crops/           the crop lists, districts and hand-authored spans

The underlying shipment records in data/raw/ are United States government
works, already in the public domain, and were never ours to license. What this
dedication adds is the editorial layer on top of them: which crops a region
shows, which growing districts count as near enough to supply it, and the
thresholds that turn weekly shipment volume into a season. Those are judgments
rather than facts, so they could otherwise carry a copyright — this waives it.

Attribution is not required. It is appreciated, and the method is written up at
https://vertumnus.fyi/about/sources so that anyone reusing the numbers can see
what they mean and where they are weak.
